        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "WORKBOX\n\nEnglish – dated 1687\n\nWood, the top and the sides of yellow silk decorated with designs in cut-paper work, painted and gilded, of stylised floral forms; on the top in the middle a panel filled with shells and a paper bird, surmounted by a bird in cut paper and flanked by the initials MW (for Mary Wright) and the date 1687. Lined in mauve silk, and partitions; inside the lid a looking-glass."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/93d0e538-be02-33dc-9aae-d942db1f92a5> .

